{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-opencode/src/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:01:07.775493Z","id":"2c59334b486cbf38b2680d3219160be49c0a67504d38f30e3d50701ba849013a","body":{"detail":"to_view puts all part events after all turns, and each event's parent_id is its own message id (lines 377-418). derive_path parents the event on that message's step and makes the last step the head. Reproduced with the COMPACTION_SQL fixture from tests/compaction_roundtrip.rs: steps msg_u1, msg_a1, msg_u2, msg_a2, compaction-prt_a1_3 (parent msg_a1); head = compaction-prt_a1_3; toolpath::v1::query::dead_ends reports [msg_u2, msg_a2]. A `part.file` attachment on the first user message would make every turn after it a dead end. origin/main's derive_path had the same event-parent rule and also appended events after turns, so this is not new. It still contradicts the CHANGELOG claim that an unchained event 'cannot become an orphan head that reports every turn as a dead end'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":264},"end":{"line":270},"content_hash":"ddeb17740fdd1c419bbc2f9e99442575aeefff1f9eec5b7917d17966266168ee"},"suggested_fix":"Interleave each part event right after its message's turn in `items` (the part belongs to that message), or keep parts in a trailing run but leave parent_id None so derive chains them after the last turn.","summary":"Pre-existing on main: an opencode session with a compaction, retry, file or agent part derives with that event as the path head and every later turn as a dead end","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-opencode/src/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:08:39.606079Z","id":"e04d76e3055e708f0a53c7775d9ee992fb18702ab3218a76b7a67adfe1b299d1","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath-opencode/src/provider.rs:264-270 chains all events after all turns, and each event's parent_id is its message id (lines 377-418). crates/toolpath-convo/src/derive.rs:439-445 resolves a recorded parent_id directly, and derive.rs:485 makes the last step the head. So with COMPACTION_SQL the compaction event (parent msg_a1) is the head, and msg_u2/msg_a2 are not its ancestors. origin/main did the same: events came after turns (origin/main provider.rs:273) and derive.rs:388-394 resolved parent_id the same way, with head = last step at line 424. Small correction: the CHANGELOG sentence covers only events with no parent or an unresolvable one, so these chained events do not strictly contradict it. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"2c59334b486cbf38b2680d3219160be49c0a67504d38f30e3d50701ba849013a","summary":"confirmed: pre-existing on main: an opencode part event (compaction, file, retry, agent) becomes the path head, and every later turn becomes a dead end","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
